To incorporate the RNFR (Rename From) and RNTO (Rename To) commands into the sequence of client requests, you would typically want to use these commands after you have created a directory (or file) that you would like to rename. 

Here’s how you can modify the sequence to include RNFR and RNTO commands. In this example, I will assume that you want to rename the directory "test" to "new_test":

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
MKD test
RNFR test
RNTO new_test
QUIT
```

In this modified sequence:
- After the `MKD test` command, which creates a directory named "test", the `RNFR test` command specifies that you want to rename "test".
- The `RNTO new_test` command specifies the new name for the directory, which is "new_test".
- Finally, the `QUIT` command ends the session. 

Make sure to adjust the names as necessary based on your specific requirements

